{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"793","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Presents in Bankopolis"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bankopolis is an incredible city in which all the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" crossroads are located on a straight line and numbered from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" along it. On each crossroad there is a bank office."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The crossroads are connected with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" oriented bicycle lanes (the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th lane goes from crossroad "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ui"},{"kind":"text","text":" to crossroad "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vi"},{"kind":"text","text":"), the difficulty of each of the lanes is known."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Oleg the bank client wants to gift happiness and joy to the bank employees. He wants to visit exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" offices, in each of them he wants to gift presents to the employees."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem is that Oleg don't want to see the reaction on his gifts, so he can't use a bicycle lane which passes near the office in which he has already presented his gifts (formally, the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th lane passes near the office on the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th crossroad if and only if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"min(ui, vi) < x < max(ui, vi)))"},{"kind":"text","text":". Of course, in each of the offices Oleg can present gifts exactly once. Oleg is going to use exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" bicycle lane to move between offices. Oleg can start his path from any office and finish it in any office."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Oleg wants to choose such a path among possible ones that the total difficulty of the lanes he will use is minimum possible. Find this minimum possible total difficulty."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, k ≤ 80"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of crossroads (and offices) and the number of offices Oleg wants to visit."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ m ≤ 2000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of bicycle lanes in Bankopolis."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain information about the lanes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of these lines contains three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ui"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vi"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ui, vi ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ci ≤ 1000"},{"kind":"text","text":"), denoting the crossroads connected by the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th road and its difficulty."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the only line print the minimum possible total difficulty of the lanes in a valid path, or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if there are no valid paths."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7 4\n4\n1 6 2\n6 2 2\n2 4 2\n2 7 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 3\n4\n2 1 2\n1 3 2\n3 4 2\n4 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example Oleg visiting banks by path "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 → 6 → 2 → 4"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Path "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 → 6 → 2 → 7"},{"kind":"text","text":" with smaller difficulity is incorrect because crossroad "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 → 7"},{"kind":"text","text":" passes near already visited office on the crossroad "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"6"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example Oleg can visit banks by path "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4 → 1 → 3"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"793D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/793/problem/D"}